#: ../../source/docs/new-roll-and-pitch-tuning.rst:257
#: ec0a9346a31143eb9cdcb56c2f4db60e
msgid "Yaw Damper/SideSlip Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/new-roll-and-pitch-tuning.rst:259
#: d9c95ab2fbb442bead53c4401e9a79ae
msgid "The yaw control loop can be configured either as a simple yaw damper (good for models with inadequate fin area) or as a combined yaw damper and side-slip controller. Because control of side-slip uses measured lateral acceleration, it will only work for those models that have enough fuselage side area to produce a measurable lateral acceleration when they side-slip (an extreme example of this is an aerobatic model flying a knife-edge maneuver where all of the lift is produced by the fuselage). Gliders with slender fuselages and flying wings cannot use this feature, but can still benefit from the yaw damper provided they have a yaw control (rudder, differential airbrakes, etc)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/new-roll-and-pitch-tuning.rst:271
#: c65ab7e2646741baa98327c883e044d2
msgid "Tuning the yaw damper"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/new-roll-and-pitch-tuning.rst:273
#: 1952e714857c4323b8f63c2c53242a34
msgid "Verify that the :ref:`YAW2SRV_SLIP<YAW2SRV_SLIP>` and :ref:`YAW2SRV_INT<YAW2SRV_INT>` gain terms are set to zero, the ``YAW2SRV_RLL`` gain term is set to 1.0 and the :ref:`YAW2SRV_DAMP<YAW2SRV_DAMP>` gain term is set to zero"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/new-roll-and-pitch-tuning.rst:276
#: 7d4f564096b143adb24737f72eb6c362
msgid "Now rapidly roll the model from maximum bank angle in one direction to maximum bank angle in the opposite direction. Do this several times going in each direction and observe the yawing motion of the model. If as the wings pass through level the nose is yawed in the opposite direction to the roll (for example when rolling from left to right bank, the nose points left) then increase the value of :ref:`KFF_RDDRMIX<KFF_RDDRMIX>` gain until the yaw goes away. Do not use a value larger than 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/new-roll-and-pitch-tuning.rst:284
#: 182625778152464fbf00b5e11fa77b71
msgid "Increase :ref:`YAW2SRV_DAMP<YAW2SRV_DAMP>` in small increments of 0.05 until the yaw angle starts to oscillate. When this happens, the tail will appear to 'wag'. Halve the gain from the value that caused the oscillation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/new-roll-and-pitch-tuning.rst:287
#: 1694533880c64da0982806b67fbbc2f9
msgid "Now roll the model into and out of turns in both directions. If the model has a tendency to yaw the nose to the outside of the turn, then increase the :ref:`YAW2SRV_RLL<YAW2SRV_RLL>` gain term in increments of 0.05 from its default value of 1.0. Conversely if the model has a tendency to yaw the nose to the inside of the turn on turn entry, then reduce the :ref:`YAW2SRV_RLL<YAW2SRV_RLL>` gain term in increments of 0.01 from its default value of 1.0. If you have to go outside the range from 0.7 to 1.4, then there is something else that needs to be sorted and you should check that you have performed step 2) correctly and check your airspeed calibration if airspeed is being used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/new-roll-and-pitch-tuning.rst:299
#: d50d6cdc94dd4ca79d233dc680c37f92
msgid "Tuning the sideslip controller"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/new-roll-and-pitch-tuning.rst:301
#: ebebf7079a5542168bf159a6b73c1013
msgid "Tune the yaw damper first"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/new-roll-and-pitch-tuning.rst:302
#: 836b6ca85cad44d28e9b1168652d38f1
msgid "Bring up the tuning graph window in the mission planner and plot the lateral acceleration ay."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/new-roll-and-pitch-tuning.rst:304
#: 0b46eaea6107448694cdad9d68f0eb25
msgid "Roll the model rapidly from full bank in each direction and observe the lateral acceleration ay. If the lateral acceleration sits around zero and doesn't change when you roll into or out of turns then no side-slip control is necessary. You can finish at this point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/new-roll-and-pitch-tuning.rst:308
#: 4602b205f7784a47869cb4cdd601b9d8
msgid "Set the :ref:`YAW2SRV_INT<YAW2SRV_INT>` gain term to 1.0. If this causes the yaw angle to oscillate then halve the gain from the smallest value that causes oscillation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/new-roll-and-pitch-tuning.rst:311
#: f7c2f3b8e94f445391a41da076d044a2
msgid "If you see that the y acceleration is offset or spikes up during turns, then progressively increase the :ref:`YAW2SRV_SLIP<YAW2SRV_SLIP>` gain in steps of 0.5 until the error goes away or the yaw angle starts to oscillate. If yaw oscillation occurs, then halve the gain from the value at which caused the oscillation."
msgstr ""

